        finding_summary: 'Twelve weeks of the tested EPA/DHA fish-oil formulation increased muscle mitochondrial membrane EPA/DHA and maximal succinate-supported ROS-emission capacity without increasing the measured oxidative-damage products.'
        finding_interpretation: 'This pre/post study did not isolate EPA from DHA, establish a specific source-control mechanism, show a whole-fish effect or demonstrate that increased ROS emission was harmful.'
