              result: 'After a meal providing >60% energy from fat and five days of high-fat feeding, muscle mitochondrial H2O2-emitting potential increased; rodent antioxidant manipulations preserved insulin sensitivity.'
              effect_magnitude: 'Study-specific direction retained; no pooled estimate or ordinary-food effective dose inferred.'
              evidence_summary: 'After a meal providing >60% energy from fat and five days of high-fat feeding, muscle mitochondrial H2O2-emitting potential increased; rodent antioxidant manipulations preserved insulin sensitivity.'
              limitations: 'The meal provided 35% of daily energy; post-meal biopsy was at four hours. Small non-randomised feeding sequence and assay-specific emission; rodent causality must not be assigned to the human cohort.'
