        finding_label: 'Ketones changed oxidant responses in neuronal preparations'
        presentation: 'mechanistic-basis'
        fm_rollup: false
        finding_statement: 'A mixture of beta-hydroxybutyrate and acetoacetate reduced oxidant responses during excitotoxic stress in rat neuronal and isolated-mitochondrial preparations, with increased NADH oxidation.'
        finding_summary: 'A mixture of beta-hydroxybutyrate and acetoacetate reduced oxidant responses during excitotoxic stress in rat neuronal and isolated-mitochondrial preparations, with increased NADH oxidation.'
        finding_interpretation: 'The experiment tested a mixture, not either constituent alone or a ketogenic food intervention; fluorescence and preparation context constrain source attribution.'
        synthesised_evidence_confidence: 'not-yet-scored'
        synthesis: 'A mixture of beta-hydroxybutyrate and acetoacetate reduced oxidant responses during excitotoxic stress in rat neuronal and isolated-mitochondrial preparations, with increased NADH oxidation.'
        synthesis_limitations: 'The experiment tested a mixture, not either constituent alone or a ketogenic food intervention; fluorescence and preparation context constrain source attribution.'
