              factorStates:
                D: 'established'
                B: 'established'
                P: 'established'
                R: 'established'
              process: 'Codex SEC Pilot 2: bounded primary Methods/Results appraisal and Scite-assisted recovery, version 1; no human scientific review recorded'
              methodology:
                name: 'Existing SEC calibration rubric proposal'
                source: 'system/reviews/sec-calibration/SEC-calibration-rubric-proposal.html'
              stoppingRationale: 'Scite full-text retrieval and citation discovery were followed by publisher/repository searches. Full pivotal Methods/Results were recovered for all four Findings. Reviews, citation counts and supporting-citation labels were not counted as replication. Stop after recovering the load-bearing reports and the material null comparison; further broad searching is not proportionate to this pilot.'
              id: 'glycaemic-sf4-assessment-v1'
              findingId: 'PM2-F4'
              title: 'Walking breaks and acute glucose exposure'
              canonicalProposition: 'Brief walking interruptions reduced postprandial glucose and insulin exposure versus continuous sitting.'
              proposition: 'Brief walking interruptions reduced postprandial glucose and insulin exposure versus continuous sitting.'
              scopeNote: 'Nineteen overweight/obese adults without diabetes; randomised three-period crossover, two-minute light/moderate walks every 20 minutes versus uninterrupted sitting. Five-hour incremental area under the curve after a standard carbohydrate/fat drink, not continuous glucose variability or insulin sensitivity.'
              factors:
                D: 2
                B: 2
                P: 1
                R: 1
              rawScore: 6
              adjustedScore: 6
              capRationale: 'No existing ceiling is triggered: raw and adjusted 6/8. Partial replication is explicitly limited to the glucose component. This score cannot be transferred to daylong variability or dietary interventions.'
              rationale:
                D: 'The laboratory crossover directly tested the walking/sitting contrast and acute glucose/insulin exposure in the stated population.'
                B: 'Independent computer-generated balanced sequence, third-party sealed-envelope allocation, blinded laboratory/statistician, supervised activity, standardised drink, period-adjusted repeated-measures models and greater-than-six-day washout provide design-appropriate protection. Three withdrawals were explained; complete-case analysis and no formal carryover test remain documented limitations rather than a demonstrated critical flaw.'
                P: 'Adjusted glucose and insulin exposure contrasts support the acute direction; confidence intervals, repeated-measures analysis and an a priori power calculation were available. Small sample and uncertainty in magnitude/transportability retain Precision 1, not a sample-size-based Bias downgrade.'
                R: 'Independent Bedfordshire investigators (Bailey and Locke) tested a separate sample with the same two-minute/every-20-minute walking contrast and supported lower five-hour glucose exposure. Different population and total rather than incremental area, plus no insulin measurement, warrant partial credit under the existing anchor, not full replication of the joint glucose/insulin claim. Independent replication was not established in this assessment. This limitation concerns the complete joint proposition, not the verified partial glucose corroboration.'
              limitations:
                0: 'The tested endpoint was acute exposure after a laboratory drink, not daylong glycaemic variability.'
                1: 'No inference to equivalent dietary effects, cognition or ADHD symptoms; the trial does not identify glucose production versus disposal.'
              sources:
                supporting:
                  0: 'dunstan_sitting_breaks_2012'
                contradictory:
                contextual:
                contradictoryAssessment: 'Bailey and Locke (2015) partially corroborates glucose, not insulin. Bailey et al. (2022) found null free-living 24-hour glucose and coefficient-of-variation effects under a different four-day regimen; this limits transportability, not the original acute contrast.'
                targetedChecks:
                  0:
                    doi: '10.2337/dc11-1931'
                    role: 'Supporting randomised intervention'
                    access: 'Original full article recovered through its ResearchGate copy; Methods/Results appraised'
                    assessment: 'Allocation, masking, washout, missingness and statistics examined. Primary report: https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3329818/ . Repository recovery: https://www.researchgate.net/publication/221870609_Breaking_Up_Prolonged_Sitting_Reduces_Postprandial_Glucose_and_Insulin_Responses'
                  1:
                    doi: '10.1016/j.jsams.2014.03.008'
                    role: 'Supporting, independent partial corroboration of glucose only'
                    access: 'Accepted author manuscript recovered from University of Bedfordshire repository; Methods/Results and limitations appraised'
                    assessment: 'Separate UK team and ten-person sample, two-minute walks every 20 minutes, lower five-hour glucose area; standing was null and insulin was not measured. Not full replication of both outcomes. https://researchportal.beds.ac.uk/p/en/research-outputs/breaking-up-prolonged-sitting-with-light-intensity-walking-improv-4'
                  2:
                    doi: '10.3390/nu14030605'
                    role: 'Contextual null evidence, not exact-protocol contradiction or replication'
                    access: 'Scite full-text design, statistical analysis and Results appraised'
                    assessment: 'Twelve overweight/obese adults, two four-day free-living regimens; no significant regimen effect on 24-hour mean, exposure or coefficient of variation. Non-significance is not equivalence.'
                retrievalLimited:
              recommendation: 'Keep the existing separation of acute exposure from volatility. Any practical sequence, food or preparation recommendation needs its own tested evidence.'
              history:
                0:
                  date: '2026-10-18'
                  decision: 'Initial appraisal considered only the original supporting trial. Bounded recovery then verified independent partial glucose corroboration in Bailey and Locke; Replication 1 gives final initial Codex-assessed provisional 6/8. Different-regimen free-living null evidence remains contextual.'
