          recordVersion: 2
          pmId: 'BRS4-FM2-PM5'
          findingId: 'PM5-F2'
          title: 'Ubiquinol has a local antioxidant role distinct from electron transport'
          proposition: 'Reduced CoQ10 inhibited induced lipid peroxidation in beef-heart submitochondrial particles even after vitamin E removal, demonstrating a local protective chemistry separate from its electron-carrier role.'
          assessmentStatus: 'codex-provisional'
          assessmentComplete: true
          lastEvidenceAssessmentDate: '2026-10-24'
          recordedOn: '2026-10-24'
          process: 'Codex bounded SEC follow-up v2: targeted primary Results/Methods recovery, exact-proposition precision and replication appraisal; no default factors, dietary inference or human review inferred.'
          methodology:
            name: 'Existing SEC four-factor anchors and integrated caps'
            version: '2026-10-24-pm4-pm5-followup-v2'
            source: 'system/reviews/sec-calibration/SEC-calibration-rubric-proposal.html#sec-assessment-status'
          factors:
            D: 2
            B: 1
            P: 1
            R: 1
          factorStates:
            D: 'established'
            B: 'established'
            P: 'established'
            R: 'established'
          rationale:
            D: 'Forsmark primary indexed Results, Table I and Figures 1–3 descriptions directly compare extraction/reconstitution in beef-heart submitochondrial particles with no HPLC-detectable vitamin E; this is the exact local chemistry claim, not oral CoQ delivery.'
            B: 'Matched extraction/reconstitution, HPLC composition checks and convergent oxygen-consumption/MDA assays address material identity and nonspecific suppression. Residual protein-bound CoQ, extraction-induced changes, missing biological-batch/dispersion reporting and artificial oxidation remain important concerns (B1).'
            P: 'Recovered Results describe loss and return of oxidation inhibition with extraction/re-addition, near-complete MDA suppression in the relevant reduced-CoQ condition, and absent detectable vitamin E. These controlled qualitative contrasts discriminate a protective capacity from its absence. Effect-size dispersion, detection limits and reproducibility across biological preparations remain uncertain (P1, not P2); no confidence intervals are fabricated.'
            R: 'Independent Yamamoto/Komuro/Niki 1990 and Frei/Kim/Ames 1990 primary experiments corroborate ubiquinol-10 antiperoxidative activity in defined liposomes without requiring co-supplied tocopherol. They differ from Forsmark mitochondrial particles and do not independently reproduce its complete extraction protocol. R1 credits partial mechanism confirmation only.'
          rawScore: 5
          adjustedScore: 5
          capRationale: 'D2/B1/P1/R1 raw 5; no D1/B0/P0 cap applies; adjusted 5. No unapproved extra downgrade.'
          limitations:
            0: 'Reconstitution is not dietary delivery. Endogenous CoQ synthesis, oxidised/reduced forms, supplement formulation, tissue uptake and membrane antioxidant activity are distinct relationships. A mitochondrial-disease trial showed only limited effects and did not establish local antioxidant mediation.'
            1: 'Recover and appraise full figure-level quantitative reporting and independent historical particle experiments for the exact vitamin-E-independent proposition.'
          sources:
            supporting:
              0: 'brs4_forsmark1991_20261023'
            contextual:
              0: 'brs4_glover2010_20261023'
            targetedChecks:
              0:
                doi: '10.1016/0014-5793(91)80720-n'
                role: 'supporting exact scoped proposition'
                access: 'Primary abstract examined; PMID2065780. No full-method concentrations extracted.'
                assessment: 'Ubiquinol inhibited lipid peroxidation even without vitamin E. Isolated particle chemistry; no oral delivery, tissue dose or human outcome.'
              1:
                doi: '10.1002/mus.21758'
                role: 'contextual; not independent replication of the core mechanism'
                access: 'Primary abstract retrieved from Europe PMC/PubMed; no unavailable full-method quantities inferred.'
                assessment: 'Small effects on exercise aerobic capacity and post-exercise lactate; other clinically relevant variables did not improve. Not proof of mitochondrial membrane protection or ordinary-food efficacy; disease/formulation-specific exposure.'
              2:
                doi: '10.3177/jnsv.36.505'
                role: 'supporting partial replication; independent liposomal chemistry, not mitochondrial-particle protocol'
                access: 'Primary PubMed/J-STAGE abstract; Scite body is only a 683-character proof note and was NOT treated as full Methods/Results'
                assessment: 'Yamamoto et al. (1990): reduced ubiquinol inhibits oxidation in defined phosphatidylcholine liposomes; oxidised ubiquinone lacks this activity. Model difference retained.'
              3:
                doi: '10.1073/pnas.87.12.4879'
                role: 'supporting partial replication; independent defined-liposome chemistry'
                access: 'Scite linear primary body, first 8000 characters: Introduction/Methods; primary PubMed abstract for results'
                assessment: 'Frei et al. (1990): purified components, controlled radical initiation and HPLC measurements support direct lipid antiperoxidative chemistry; not an independent submitochondrial-particle protocol.'
              4:
                doi: '10.1016/0014-5793(91)80720-n'
                role: 'supporting; recovered original indexed Results and Table I'
                access: 'Publisher PDF indexed Results/Methods passages; original complete PDF not downloaded'
                assessment: 'Forsmark et al. (1991): extraction removes detectable CoQ and tocopherol; re-addition restores the relevant respiratory/antiperoxidative contrasts. Residual bound CoQ acknowledged in the primary Results.'
            retrievalLimited:
              0:
                url: 'https://doi.org/10.1016/0014-5793(91)80720-n'
                limitation: 'Complete original PDF, biological-batch counts and curve-level dispersion not recovered. P1 is based on controlled qualitative discrimination, not a precise efficacy magnitude; no P2 credit.'
            contradictoryAssessment: 'Kagan et al. (1990) proposed tocopherol recycling as mediation; Forsmark directly tested removal/re-addition. Independent model-membrane studies support a direct antiperoxidative component. This does not deny tocopherol synergy or prooxidant reactions under other conditions.'
          evidenceLocations:
            0: 'Forsmark 1991 abstract and primary PDF page 39 methods'
            1: 'Glover 2010 clinical trial abstract (context only)'
            2: 'Forsmark indexed original Results p40: Table I and Figures 1–3 descriptions'
            3: 'Yamamoto 1990 primary abstract and Frei 1990 primary Methods/abstract'
          history:
            0:
              date: '2026-10-24'
              decision: 'User authorised SEC completion for approved PM4/PM5 reassessment. New versioned assessment; propositions, admissions, original confidence storage and all prior SEC records preserved. This is not qualified human scientific review.'
            1:
              date: '2026-10-24'
              decision: 'User requested investigation of all four remaining unscored Findings. Version 1 preserved unchanged; this version records recovered evidence and remaining essential gaps.'
      83:
        sha256: '95d81ea0d19bb488b9e3c63ecaf097106883c31619473726597c1defef6f6453'
        record:
          id: 'brs4-pm5-pm5-f5-sec'
          recordVersion: 2
          pmId: 'BRS4-FM2-PM5'
          findingId: 'PM5-F5'
          title: 'Sulforaphane protected mitochondria in defined cell experiments'
          proposition: 'Sulforaphane pretreatment protected mitochondrial lipids, proteins and enzyme activities in oxidant-challenged SH-SY5Y cells through an Nrf2-dependent mechanism; separate vascular-cell experiments measured induction of mitochondrial defences.'
          assessmentStatus: 'not-scored'
          assessmentComplete: false
          lastEvidenceAssessmentDate: '2026-10-24'
          recordedOn: '2026-10-24'
          process: 'Codex bounded SEC follow-up v2: targeted primary Results/Methods recovery, exact-proposition precision and replication appraisal; no default factors, dietary inference or human review inferred.'
          methodology:
            name: 'Existing SEC four-factor anchors and integrated caps'
            version: '2026-10-24-pm4-pm5-followup-v2'
            source: 'system/reviews/sec-calibration/SEC-calibration-rubric-proposal.html#sec-assessment-status'
          factors:
            D: 2
            R: 0
          factorStates:
            D: 'established'
            B: 'unresolved'
            P: 'unresolved'
            R: 'established'
          rationale:
            D: 'Oliveira measures mitochondrial lipid/protein injury and Nrf2 dependence after the stated pretreatment/challenge; Zhu measures the separately described defence induction.'
            B: 'Publisher preview and Scite supply only the abstract for the pivotal Oliveira study. It reports Nrf2 silencing, but non-targeting/knockdown controls, assay validation, biological repeat independence and reporting protections remain unverified. Public figure recovery returned HTML, not a usable figure; no B1/B0 is assigned by default.'
            P: 'No primary figure-level replicate counts, dispersion or dose/knockdown contrasts were recovered. The public abstract and other cell-model studies cannot supply those quantities for the exact SH-SY5Y/H2O2/Nrf2 proposition. Precision remains unresolved rather than P0.'
            R: 'One verified experimental line tests the exact SH-SY5Y injury/Nrf2 proposition. Zhu vascular-cell defence induction differs in model and endpoint and is not exact replication.'
          capRationale: 'No complete total: essential unresolved factors remain; unknown is not zero.'
          limitations:
            0: 'This supports preclinical mechanism engagement. Human broccoli-sprout pharmacokinetics establish absorption mainly as conjugated metabolites, not equivalence to sustained free sulforaphane in culture or demonstrated mitochondrial protection from a food.'
            1: 'Recover Oliveira full results, replicate structure, knockdown controls and uncertainty. Keep food absorption evidence separate from protective efficacy.'
          sources:
            supporting:
              0: 'brs4_oliveira2018_20261023'
              1: 'brs4_zhu2008_20261023'
            contextual:
            targetedChecks:
              0:
                doi: '10.1007/s12035-017-0684-2'
                role: 'supporting exact scoped proposition'
                access: 'Primary abstract retrieved from Europe PMC/PubMed; no unavailable full-method quantities inferred.'
                assessment: 'Mitochondrial membrane lipid peroxidation, protein carbonylation/nitration and enzyme inhibition were attenuated; Nrf2 silencing abolished protection. Cell line, imposed oxidant stress and free-compound exposure; not broccoli or human neuronal target engagement.'
              1:
                doi: '10.1007/s12012-008-9020-4'
                role: 'supporting exact scoped proposition'
                access: 'Primary abstract retrieved from Europe PMC/PubMed; no unavailable full-method quantities inferred.'
                assessment: 'Sulforaphane induced cellular and mitochondrial antioxidant defences and increased resistance to imposed oxidative/electrophilic stress. Mitochondrial defence induction is not the same endpoint as direct mitochondrial membrane injury; not an independent neuronal replication.'
            retrievalLimited:
              0:
                url: 'https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s12035-017-0684-2'
                limitation: 'Publisher subscription preview and Scite abstract fallback only; usable complete Results/Methods not recovered.'
            contradictoryAssessment: 'No exact-proposition contradiction was established in this bounded appraisal. Nonmatching endpoints and tissue/exposure limits remain explicit; this is not an exhaustive absence-of-contradiction claim.'
          evidenceLocations:
            0: 'Oliveira 2018 primary abstract, PMID28730528'
            1: 'Zhu 2008 primary abstract, PMID18607771 (distinct endpoint)'
            2: 'Publisher preview and Scite source=abstract/contentDenied=true; figure download returned HTML, not scientific data.'
          followUp: 'Obtain an authorised full text or author manuscript (Methods, mitochondrial injury figures and Nrf2-silencing controls). Establish biological replicates and uncertainty. No food-effect or human translation conclusion follows from resolving these cellular factors.'
          history:
            0:
              date: '2026-10-24'
              decision: 'User authorised SEC completion for approved PM4/PM5 reassessment. New versioned assessment; propositions, admissions, original confidence storage and all prior SEC records preserved. This is not qualified human scientific review.'
            1:
              date: '2026-10-24'
              decision: 'User requested investigation of all four remaining unscored Findings. Version 1 preserved unchanged; this version records recovered evidence and remaining essential gaps.'
  actual:
    schemaVersion: 1
    assessments:
      0:
        sha256: '31d36a31a826ee822e206ee310e89878267dcde58899b2ec1210e2529e34831a'
        record:
          recordVersion: 5
          id: 'gaba-sf1-assessment-v1'
          pmId: 'BRS1-FM4-PM9'
          findingId: 'PM9-F1'
          assessmentStatus: 'conditional'
          recordedOn: '2026-10-17'
          lastEvidenceAssessmentDate: '2026-10-18'
          process: 'Codex-assisted bounded reassessment: existing four-study abstract synthesis plus complete Kaufman 1991 text via Scite; formal assessment unresolved; no expert-review completion inferred'
          methodology:
            name: 'SEC calibration rubric proposal'
            source: 'system/reviews/sec-calibration/SEC-calibration-rubric-proposal.html'
          status: 'Conditional SEC estimate — under calibration: 4/8 · Low–Moderate; formal SEC Not scored'
          canonicalProposition: 'GABA synthesis requires pyridoxal-5-phosphate as the glutamate decarboxylase coenzyme, and because GAD65 exists substantially as apoenzyme while GAD67 is largely holoenzyme, cofactor availability governs reserve synthesis capacity more than basal output.'
          proposition: 'GAD65 and GAD67 differ in their typical PLP-bound states, providing experimental evidence for distinct modes of regulating GABA synthesis. The larger apoenzyme fraction associated with GAD65 suggests potentially recruitable catalytic capacity. However, independent replication of the specific occupancy finding has not yet been established in this assessment, and the physiological importance of this proposed reserve mechanism in the human brain remains uncertain.'
          factors:
            D: 1
          conditional:
            factors:
              D: 1
              B: 1
              P: 1
              R: 1
            rawScore: 4
            adjustedScore: 4
            label: 'Low–Moderate'
            statuses:
              D: 'Established inferential bridge for the approved proposition'
              B: 'Conditional'
              P: 'Conditional'
              R: 'Conditional'
            qualification: 'Conditional SEC estimate — under calibration. B1/P1/R1 require verification; this is not an approved confidence assessment.'
            caps: 'D1 invokes the existing provisional ceiling of 5/8; the conditional raw total of 4 remains 4/8. No undocumented decrement is applied. Formal totals remain uncalculated.'
          rationale:
            D: '1 — Rat-brain extracts directly assess apoenzyme identity/occupancy. Recruitable physiological capacity remains an inference, particularly for the human brain. Curated reaction chemistry does not close that bridge.'
            B: 'Conditional 1 — Kaufman 1991 full methods describe isoform-selective immunoprecipitation, immunoblot verification, negative staining controls and triplicate activity assays with/without added PLP. The authors acknowledge co-precipitation of the other isoform, plausibly through heterodimers. Martin 1991 supplies orthogonal identification controls at abstract level, but its full methods and handling effects remain unverified. These residual concerns prevent B2; this is not evidence of a critical flaw.'
            P: 'Conditional 1 — Kaufman reports a 2.2-fold PLP response for GAD65 versus a slight GAD67 response, with the table caption specifying SEM and n=4. The recovered text lacks numerical table cells and does not establish whether n=4 represents independent preparations. The qualitative distinction is informative, but exact occupancy uncertainty and human reserve magnitude remain unverified; no interval is invented.'
            R: 'Conditional 1 — Kaufman/Houser/Tobin and Martin/Martin/Wu/Espina are distinct author groups using immunoprecipitation/activity and radiolabel approaches. Their rodent observations partially corroborate differential cofactor occupancy, not demonstrated human reserve recruitment. Shared antibody resources, preparation independence and the full Martin protocol remain incompletely assessed; the 1979/1985 studies and 1993 review are not extra replications. Independent replication was not established in this assessment. This refers to the complete assessed proposition, not a denial of partial biochemical corroboration.'
          sources:
            supporting:
              0: 'martin_regulation_1993'
            contradictory:
            contradictoryAssessment: 'No contradictory evidence verified in the bounded assessment; literature-wide absence is not established.'
            contextual:
              0: 'bayoumi_vitamin_b6_deficiency_1972'
              1: 'erecinska_regulation_1996'
              2: 'zhang_decreased_carbon_2015'
              3: 'cataldo_comprehensive_2024'
              4: 'abedrabbo_classical_2026'
            targetedChecks:
              0:
                doi: '10.1111/j.1471-4159.1991.tb08211.x'
                role: 'Supporting primary experiment; partial corroboration'
                access: 'Scite full text read in full; numerical table cells absent from extracted text'
                assessment: 'Kaufman, Houser and Tobin 1991: mouse-brain activity after isoform-selective immunoprecipitation, with/without PLP, plus rat localisation. GAD65 responds 2.2-fold; GAD67 responds slightly. Caption reports SEM, n=4; biological independence and exact uncertainty not established. Co-precipitation acknowledged. Supports occupancy differences, not observed human physiological reserve or dietary response.'
              1:
                doi: '10.1523/jneurosci.11-09-02725.1991'
                role: 'Supporting'
                access: 'Scite abstract only; truncated at 250 words'
                assessment: 'Rat regions and synaptosomes: labelled PLP plus orthogonal biochemical identification controls; supports the occupancy/apoenzyme observation, not demonstrated human reserve function.'
              2:
                doi: '10.1042/bj2310695'
                role: 'Contextual / related'
                access: 'Scite abstract only'
                assessment: 'Pig-brain alpha/beta/gamma forms differ kinetically. These forms are not automatically equivalent to GAD65/GAD67 occupancy; not a verified independent replication. Author overlap includes S. J. Wu with the 1991 study.'
              3:
                doi: '10.1111/j.1471-4159.1979.tb05274.x'
                role: 'Contextual / related'
                access: 'Scite abstract only'
                assessment: 'Rat enzyme activation responds to PLP and phosphate across preparation conditions. Supports regulation in vitro, not the exact isoform occupancy claim. Martin laboratory overlap prevents counting it as independent replication.'
              4:
                doi: '10.1111/j.1471-4159.1993.tb03165.x'
                role: 'Supporting synthesis'
                access: 'Scite abstract only'
                assessment: 'Existing review synthesises occupancy and reserve interpretation; is not a new independent experiment. GAD67 also contributes apoenzyme, preventing an absolute apo/holo dichotomy.'
            retrievalLimited:
              0:
                doi: '10.1111/j.1471-4159.1991.tb08211.x'
                url: 'https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1471-4159.1991.tb08211.x'
                limitation: 'Earlier abstract-only gap partly recovered through Scite full text. Missing numerical table cells and preparation-level definition of n=4 affect P/R; no invented error bounds.'
              1:
                doi: '10.1523/jneurosci.11-09-02725.1991'
                url: 'https://www.jneurosci.org/content/jneuro/11/9/2725.full.pdf'
                limitation: 'Earlier publisher PDF retrieval returned HTTP 403. Recheck: Scite still supplies a truncated abstract; PMC recovery encountered an access challenge. Missing full methods and occupancy uncertainty affect B/P/R; inaccessibility is not negative evidence.'
          limitations:
            0: 'Exact occupancy uncertainty, independent preparation counts and replication of the complete reserve proposition remain unverified; B/P/R are conditional.'
            1: 'Human physiological importance of the proposed reserve mechanism remains uncertain.'
            2: 'No inference of increased human brain GABA synthesis from dietary B6 above adequacy.'
          stoppingRationale: 'Stopped after recovering the previously identified Kaufman primary study and rechecking Martin access. Partial biochemical corroboration supports a bounded conditional estimate; remaining table/method and human-physiology gaps cannot be resolved by counting contextual papers or curated records.'
          history:
            0:
              date: '2026-10-17'
              decision: 'Version 1: distinguished evidence weakness from retrieval limitations; all four factors unresolved and formal SEC Not scored. No scientific admission changed.'
            1:
              date: '2026-10-17'
              decision: 'Version 2: targeted Scite abstract checks support provisional D1/B1. Formal P/R remain unresolved. Added conditional P1/R1 scenario yielding working estimate 4/8, not a formal score. Adopted the user-approved narrower conclusion; no admission changed.'
            2:
              date: '2026-10-17'
              decision: 'Version 3: withdrew the conditional numerical estimate from current presentation. Retained Not scored, unresolved P/R and the exact approved conclusion shared with SF1. Version 2 scenario is superseded history only.'
            3:
              date: '2026-10-17'
              decision: 'Version 4: reassessed under the same conditional/established distinction as SF2 after recovering Kaufman 1991 full text. Display conditional D1/B1/P1/R1 = 4/8 Low–Moderate; formal B/P/R and totals remain unresolved. Preserved versions 1–3, approved conclusion, sources and dietary boundaries. Earlier abstract-level B1 is now explicitly conditional, not a completed bias appraisal.'
            4:
              date: '2026-10-18'
              decision: 'Version 5 calibration review: retained conditional 4/8, not accepted provisional SEC. D1 reflects the reserve-capacity inference, not an automatic animal-study penalty. B1/P1/R1 remain bounded hypotheses based on examined controls, qualitative response and partial corroboration; they are not substitutes for missing methods, uncertainty or independence checks. No new retrieval, scope change or promotion; prior history preserved.'
          factorStates:
            D: 'established'
            B: 'conditional'
            P: 'conditional'
            R: 'conditional'
