                      population: 'Children and adults with ADHD and age-matched control participants.'
                      result: 'GABA differences between ADHD and control groups varied with age: the paediatric reduction was not reproduced in adults, in whom GABA was higher.'
                      effect_magnitude: 'An age-by-group interaction in GABA level rather than a single group contrast.'
                      evidence_summary: 'Contradicts a uniform GABA deficit account of ADHD and establishes age dependence of the concentration difference.'
                      limitations: 'Concentration rather than synthesis; cross-sectional age comparison rather than longitudinal; Edden is a co-author, so this is not fully independent of the paediatric reports it qualifies.'
