          id: 'glycaemic-sf1-assessment-v1'
          findingId: 'PM2-F1'
          title: 'Short training and glucose excursions'
          canonicalProposition: 'Seven days of aerobic training reduced excursion frequency, magnitude and duration in type 2 diabetes.'
          proposition: 'In an uncontrolled cohort of 13 sedentary adults with type 2 diabetes, seven days of aerobic training were associated with lower glucose range and selected excursion measures; high-glucose excursion frequency and duration remained statistically inconclusive.'
          scopeNote: 'Scoped observed change in 13 sedentary adults with type 2 diabetes: baseline monitoring versus the final days of seven supervised exercise sessions. No causal attribution, universal exercise effect or all-endpoint improvement is asserted.'
          factors:
            D: 2
            B: 1
            P: 1
            R: 0
          rawScore: 4
          adjustedScore: 4
          capRationale: 'No existing cap triggered for the explicitly observational before/after proposition. The prior causal all-endpoint claim remains archived at adjusted 2/8; no controls were added.'
          rationale:
            D: 'Continuous glucose monitoring in the stated diabetes cohort directly measured excursions before and during the specified training period. Direct measurement does not establish causal attribution.'
            B: 'For the scoped observed cohort change, controlled meals, supervised sessions and within-person monitoring provide partial protection; time trends, selection and no concurrent control preclude a causal interpretation. Bias Protection 1 applies only after the claim was explicitly narrowed, not retroactively to the old causal claim.'
            P: 'Observed range and selected low-glucose measures changed; high-glucose frequency (p=0.07) and duration (p=0.06) remain inconclusive. The revised proposition preserves those distinctions. Small-cohort endpoint and magnitude uncertainty warrants Precision 1, not a claim of universal improvement or equivalence.'
            R: 'Only one supporting empirical line for the exact population, protocol and endpoint was verified after bounded primary-source and Scite citation screening. Independent replication was not established in this assessment. This is not a claim that replication is absent from the entire literature; related protocols do not earn replication credit automatically.'
          limitations:
            0: 'Uncontrolled before/after association, not demonstrated exercise causation or all-endpoint improvement.'
            1: 'No cognitive or ADHD endpoint; a null 24-hour mean does not negate endpoint-specific excursion changes.'
          sources:
            supporting:
              0: 'mikus_2012_22311420'
            contradictory:
            contextual:
              0: 'zametkin_cerebral_1990'
              1: 'di_girolamo_prevalence_2022'
            contradictoryAssessment: 'Mixed outcomes within the pivotal dataset limit the claim; no verified independent exact-protocol contradictory trial was identified in this bounded assessment.'
