            B: 'Randomised within-person design and matched source/quantity reduce confounding. Visible texture and consumption-time differences remain; concealment and assay masking were not demonstrated in recovered methods. No critical systematic error was established.'
            P: 'Reported tracer effect and standard errors support the directional finding, but n=10, no extracted paired interval and negative secondary outcomes limit magnitude and extrapolation; nulls are not scored as equivalence.'
            R: 'The bounded exact-protocol search and source appraisal yielded one empirical dataset; thesis/journal reports and other processing studies are not independent replications. Independent replication was not established in this assessment.'
          limitations:
            0: 'One small older-male trial; no independent replication of the exact matched-beef protocol was established in this assessment. No claim that all foods should be minced or that this improves attention.'
            1: "Evidence-confidence conclusions must distinguish limitations of the underlying scientific evidence from limitations of the framework's evidence retrieval and assessment. Absence of verified evidence within an assessment must not be represented as evidence of absence."
            2: 'Intervention disposition: the matched 135 g lean-beef preparation experiment in ten older men remains scientific evidence only. No approved canonical preparation SOP or food-strategy registration is established; exact intervention scope awaits confirmation.'
