          title: 'Inactivity and training changed mitochondrial H2O2 emission'
          proposition: 'Two weeks of leg immobilisation increased muscle mitochondrial H2O2 emission at a controlled membrane potential; six weeks of aerobic retraining restored emission and ATP-generating respiration toward baseline. Acute exercise responses were respiratory-state dependent in a separate study.'
