          title: 'Vitamin E protection depends on tissue and stress context'
          proposition: 'Vitamin E deficiency and repletion experiments support a protective role for vitamin E in selected mitochondrial membranes. Mitochondrial-GPX4 loss in mice caused retinal lipid oxidation and photoreceptor loss partly ameliorated by vitamin E. Other rat liver experiments did not show the same dependence.'
          assessmentStatus: 'codex-provisional'
          assessmentComplete: true
