            B: 'Isoform-specific knockout/control comparisons, lipid assays and dietary rescue improve attribution. Small tissue/model samples, developmental effects and incomplete protection against allocation/litter-related confounding remain; tissue divergence is retained.'
            P: 'Azuma Figures 1–3 report replicate counts, variability and partial rescue with retained null cone endpoints; the direction is informative but rescue size and organelle-specific attribution remain uncertain. No numerical pooling across tissues.'
            R: 'Independent rat and mouse research lines give partial confirmation of context-dependent protective capacity with different endpoints. Liver nulls constrain rather than negate the tissue-qualified proposition; they do not warrant R2 universal protection.'
          rawScore: 4
          adjustedScore: 4
          capRationale: 'D1 ceiling 5 applies; raw 4 remains adjusted 4. No B0/P0 cap applies.'
          limitations:
            0: 'Capacity is not benefit from extra intake. Deficiency models, mitochondrial-GPX4 deletion and high supplemental exposure do not establish ordinary-food equivalence, uniform protection across tissues or cognitive benefit. Retinal lipid assays were not measurements restricted to isolated mitochondrial membranes.'
