          factorStates:
            D: 'established'
            B: 'established'
            P: 'established'
            R: 'established'
          rationale:
            D: 'Wang and Shi directly measure mitochondrial GSH and isotope-labelled organelle uptake after SLC25A39 perturbation. The scored proposition is compartmental import, not GSH antioxidant efficacy, dietary precursor success or clinical protection.'
            B: 'Independent genetic perturbations, cDNA rescue, tag/background controls, organelle separation, isotope uptake time courses and structure-function mutants address off-target, contamination and indirect synthesis explanations (Wang Fig. 3; Shi Figs 4–5). These are design-appropriate protections for this biochemical proposition.'
            P: 'Uptake contrasts, time courses and rescue/mutant comparisons with independent biological samples and LC-MS quality controls resolve the qualitative presence of an import dependency. The decision boundary is discrimination from intact uptake after knockout or merely cytosolic depletion; no precise human flux is inferred.'
            R: 'Wang (Birsoy group) and Shi (Shen group) independently establish the same SLC25A39/GSH-import relationship with distinct screens and uptake experiments. Colell is context for transport limitations, not a third SLC25A39 replication.'
          rawScore: 8
          adjustedScore: 8
          capRationale: 'No D1/B0/P0 ceiling applies; adjusted equals raw. No extra model-to-human penalty is added because the proposition remains model-specific.'
          limitations:
            0: 'Glutathione-dependent iron–sulfur-cluster maintenance is not interchangeable with peroxide detoxification. Cytosolic or blood glutathione does not establish mitochondrial delivery; in ethanol-fed rats NAC failed to restore mitochondrial GSH whereas SAM supplementation did.'
          sources:
            supporting:
              0: 'wang_slc25a39_2021'
              1: 'brs4_shi2022_20261023'
            contextual:
              0: 'brs4_fernandez1997_20261023'
