          title: 'Omega-3 exposure need not reduce mitochondrial ROS emission'
          proposition: 'Twelve weeks of the tested EPA/DHA fish-oil formulation increased muscle mitochondrial membrane EPA/DHA and maximal succinate-supported ROS-emission capacity without increasing the measured oxidative-damage products.'
          assessmentStatus: 'not-scored'
          assessmentComplete: false
          lastEvidenceAssessmentDate: '2026-10-24'
          recordedOn: '2026-10-24'
          process: 'Codex bounded SEC follow-up v2: targeted primary Results/Methods recovery, exact-proposition precision and replication appraisal; no default factors, dietary inference or human review inferred.'
