            R: 0
          factorStates:
            D: 'established'
            B: 'established'
            P: 'unresolved'
            R: 'established'
          rationale:
            D: 'Herbst directly measures the specified formulation, mitochondrial fatty acids, emission and selected damage markers before/after 12 weeks.'
            B: 'The pre/post study has no placebo arm; temporal and behavioural confounding and selective endpoint sensitivity remain. The Finding is kept as a description of measured endpoints, not a causal claim of harm or safety.'
            P: 'Re-examination locates oxidative products in Herbst Figure 5B/C: whole-muscle homogenate 4HNE and protein-carbonyl measurements, n=18, mean/SEM and paired testing. Numeric paired changes, covariance/uncertainty and a justified equivalence boundary are not recovered. A nonsignificant change cannot establish no meaningful increase. The exact existing phrase “without increasing” remains ambiguous between a descriptive test result and an absence claim; no P factor is forced.'
            R: 'One independent pre/post cohort supports the exact formulation/time/endpoint combination in the scoped appraisal; two recruitment rounds are not independent research-group replications.'
          capRationale: 'No complete total: essential unresolved factors remain; unknown is not zero.'
          limitations:
            0: 'This pre/post study did not isolate EPA from DHA, establish a specific source-control mechanism, show a whole-fish effect or demonstrate that increased ROS emission was harmful.'
            1: 'Appraise damage-marker effect estimates/uncertainty against a justified boundary; retain the descriptive non-increase without interpreting equivalence or safety.'
            2: 'Damage products were measured in muscle homogenates, not isolated mitochondrial membranes. Existing wording should be reviewed before a no-increase interpretation is scored.'
          sources:
            supporting:
              0: 'brs4_herbst2014_20261023'
            contextual:
            targetedChecks:
              0:
