            directional_finding: 'Rpe65-deficient cells were approximately 20–40-fold less photosensitive; exogenous 9-cis-retinal restored photosensitivity where melanopsin was present.'
            assessment:
              study: 'Rpe65-deficient and melanopsin-ablated mouse retinal preparations; retinal-analogue rescue.'
              population: 'Rpe65-deficient and melanopsin-ablated mouse retinal preparations; retinal-analogue rescue.'
              result: 'Rpe65-deficient cells were approximately 20–40-fold less photosensitive; exogenous 9-cis-retinal restored photosensitivity where melanopsin was present.'
              effect_magnitude: 'Rpe65-deficient cells were approximately 20–40-fold less photosensitive; exogenous 9-cis-retinal restored photosensitivity where melanopsin was present.'
              evidence_summary: 'Rpe65-deficient cells were approximately 20–40-fold less photosensitive; exogenous 9-cis-retinal restored photosensitivity where melanopsin was present.'
