      - id: PM2-F1
        finding_label: Short training and observed glucose excursions
        presentation: mechanistic-basis
        fm_rollup: false
        finding_summary: 'In an uncontrolled cohort of 13 sedentary adults with type 2 diabetes, seven days of aerobic training were associated with lower glucose range and selected excursion measures; high-glucose excursion frequency and duration remained statistically inconclusive.'
        finding_statement: 'In an uncontrolled cohort of 13 sedentary adults with type 2 diabetes, seven days of aerobic training were associated with lower glucose range and selected excursion measures; high-glucose excursion frequency and duration remained statistically inconclusive.'
        finding_interpretation: Continuous monitoring tests variability more directly than one fasting value.
        synthesis: 'In an uncontrolled cohort of 13 sedentary adults with type 2 diabetes, seven days of aerobic training were associated with lower glucose range and selected excursion measures; high-glucose excursion frequency and duration remained statistically inconclusive.'
        synthesis_limitations: 'Uncontrolled before/after association, not demonstrated exercise causation or all-endpoint improvement. No cognitive or ADHD endpoint; a null 24-hour mean does not negate endpoint-specific excursion changes.'
        synthesised_evidence_confidence: not-yet-scored
        evidence_considered:
