      - id: PM2-F3
        finding_label: Variability and oxidative stress are associated
        presentation: mechanistic-basis
        fm_rollup: false
        finding_summary: An observational diabetes study linked glucose fluctuation measures with urinary oxidative-stress markers.
        finding_statement: An observational diabetes study linked glucose fluctuation measures with urinary oxidative-stress markers.
        finding_interpretation: The association motivates assessment; it does not demonstrate that flattening glucose improves cognition.
        synthesis: The original cohort association was not reproduced in an independent better-controlled diabetes sample using mass spectrometry. Population and assay differences constrain generalisation; this is not a causal oxidative-stress claim.
        synthesis_limitations: Independent null evidence prevents presenting the association as uniformly established across type 2 diabetes. Assay and glycaemic-control differences may contribute to heterogeneity; neither causal direction nor dietary/cognitive efficacy follows.
        synthesised_evidence_confidence: not-yet-scored
        evidence_considered:
          - label: Monnier et al. (2006)
            citation_key: monnier_2006_16638903
            href: /docs/papers/BRAIN-Diet-References#monnier_2006_16638903
