      - id: PM2-F5
        finding_label: Whole-grain processing and daily variability
        finding_statement: 'In adults with type 2 diabetes, the tested less-processed whole-grain package reduced daily glucose standard deviation and mean amplitude of glycaemic excursions (MAGE) versus a nutrient-matched finely processed package over two weeks.'
        finding_summary: 'In adults with type 2 diabetes, the tested less-processed whole-grain package reduced daily glucose standard deviation and mean amplitude of glycaemic excursions (MAGE) versus a nutrient-matched finely processed package over two weeks.'
        synthesis: 'Daily glucose SD difference -0.16 mmol/L (95% CI -0.25 to -0.06); mean amplitude of glycaemic excursions (MAGE) -0.36 (-0.65 to -0.08). Time in range and CONGA were null. A food package, not an isolated grain or fibre effect; unmasked foods, short duration. Concealed randomisation, blinded CGM, initial masked analysis and intention-to-treat models support appraisal.'
        synthesis_limitations: 'A food package, not an isolated grain or fibre effect; unmasked foods, short duration. Concealed randomisation, blinded CGM, initial masked analysis and intention-to-treat models support appraisal.'
        synthesised_evidence_confidence: not-yet-scored
        evidence_considered:
          - label: Aberg et al. (2020)
            href: '#stage2-ref-aberg'
            data_level: Human Study
            evidence_source: bounded-external-search
            directional_finding: Daily glucose SD difference -0.16 mmol/L (95% CI -0.25 to -0.06); mean amplitude of glycaemic excursions (MAGE) -0.36 (-0.65 to -0.08). Time in range and CONGA were null.
            assessment:
              study: 'Two-week crossover: intact oats, brown rice and coarse/kibbled bread versus matched finely processed whole-grain products; at least two-week washout.'
              population: 31 adults with type 2 diabetes; 28 completed.
              result: Daily glucose SD difference -0.16 mmol/L (95% CI -0.25 to -0.06); mean amplitude of glycaemic excursions (MAGE) -0.36 (-0.65 to -0.08). Time in range and CONGA were null.
              limitations: 'A food package, not an isolated grain or fibre effect; unmasked foods, short duration. Concealed randomisation, blinded CGM, initial masked analysis and intention-to-treat models support appraisal.'
              retrieval_scope: Full primary Methods/Results
              effect_magnitude: Daily glucose SD difference -0.16 mmol/L (95% CI -0.25 to -0.06); mean amplitude of glycaemic excursions (MAGE) -0.36 (-0.65 to -0.08). Time in range and CONGA were null.
              evidence_summary: 'Daily glucose SD difference -0.16 mmol/L (95% CI -0.25 to -0.06); mean amplitude of glycaemic excursions (MAGE) -0.36 (-0.65 to -0.08). Time in range and CONGA were null. A food package, not an isolated grain or fibre effect; unmasked foods, short duration. Concealed randomisation, blinded CGM, initial masked analysis and intention-to-treat models support appraisal.'
            citation_key: stage2-ref-aberg
        sec_assessment_ref:
