      - id: PM2-F8
        finding_label: Vigorous activity bouts and variability
        finding_statement: Four brief vigorous bodyweight bouts daily produced small secondary continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) variability improvements over 48 hours in inactive adults with well-controlled type 2 diabetes; the primary mean-glucose contrast was not significant.
        finding_summary: Four brief vigorous bodyweight bouts daily produced small secondary continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) variability improvements over 48 hours in inactive adults with well-controlled type 2 diabetes; the primary mean-glucose contrast was not significant.
        synthesis: 'Primary mean difference -0.2 mmol/L (95% CI -0.4 to 0; p=0.07). Secondary SD -0.1 mmol/L, CV -1 percentage point and MAGE -0.3 mmol/L; time in range was null. Small secondary effects without multiplicity adjustment; short washout permits carryover. Not evidence for gentle walking or lasting clinical benefit.'
        synthesis_limitations: Small secondary effects without multiplicity adjustment; short washout permits carryover. Not evidence for gentle walking or lasting clinical benefit.
        synthesised_evidence_confidence: not-yet-scored
        evidence_considered:
          - label: Babir et al. (2026)
            href: '#stage2-ref-babir'
            data_level: Human Study
            evidence_source: bounded-external-search
            directional_finding: 'Primary mean difference -0.2 mmol/L (95% CI -0.4 to 0; p=0.07). Secondary SD -0.1 mmol/L, CV -1 percentage point and MAGE -0.3 mmol/L; time in range was null.'
            assessment:
              study: 'Two 48-hour crossover periods: four one-minute vigorous bodyweight bouts daily versus usual activity; at least one hour between bouts, encouraged after meals.'
              population: '31 inactive adults with well-controlled, non-insulin-treated type 2 diabetes.'
              result: 'Primary mean difference -0.2 mmol/L (95% CI -0.4 to 0; p=0.07). Secondary SD -0.1 mmol/L, CV -1 percentage point and MAGE -0.3 mmol/L; time in range was null.'
              limitations: Small secondary effects without multiplicity adjustment; short washout permits carryover. Not evidence for gentle walking or lasting clinical benefit.
              retrieval_scope: Full primary Methods/Results
              effect_magnitude: 'Primary mean difference -0.2 mmol/L (95% CI -0.4 to 0; p=0.07). Secondary SD -0.1 mmol/L, CV -1 percentage point and MAGE -0.3 mmol/L; time in range was null.'
              evidence_summary: 'Primary mean difference -0.2 mmol/L (95% CI -0.4 to 0; p=0.07). Secondary SD -0.1 mmol/L, CV -1 percentage point and MAGE -0.3 mmol/L; time in range was null. Small secondary effects without multiplicity adjustment; short washout permits carryover. Not evidence for gentle walking or lasting clinical benefit.'
            citation_key: stage2-ref-babir
