o -0.08). Time in range and CONGA were null.","limitations":"A food package, not an isolated grain or fibre effect; unmasked foods, short duration. Concealed randomisation, blinded CGM, initial masked analysis and intention-to-treat models support appraisal.","retrieval_scope":"Full primary Methods/Results","effect_magnitude":"Daily glucose SD difference -0.16 mmol/L (95% CI -0.25 to -0.06); mean amplitude of glycaemic excursions (MAGE) -0.36 (-0.65 to -0.08). Time in range and CONGA were null.","evidence_summary":"Daily glucose SD difference -0.16 mmol/L (95% CI -0.25 to -0.06); mean amplitude of glycaemic excursions (MAGE) -0.36 (-0.65 to -0.08). Time in range and CONGA were null. A food package, not an isolated grain or fibre effect; unmasked foods, short duration. Concealed randomisation, blinded CGM, initial masked analysis and intention-to-treat models support appraisal."},"citation_key":"stage2-ref-aberg","canonical_reference":{"author_year":"Aberg et al. (2020)","number":7,"anchor":"#pm-ref-7"}}],"sec_assessment_ref":{"id":"glycaemic-f5-assessment-v1","version":2,"sha256":"85c5ad88e1ad23cade683e5a6b84344dd53ad252166c3732d11653eb8be8b55e"},"connected_supportive_evidence":[]}} pmId={"BRS6-FM1-PM2"} />
    
