nket superiority to all continuous exercise.","retrieval_scope":"Full publisher PDF Methods, Table 1 and Results","effect_magnitude":"MAGE decreased 1.7 +/- 0.4 mmol/L within interval training; interval/control comparison p=0.01. Within-period mean glucose was inconclusive (p=0.08).","evidence_summary":"MAGE decreased 1.7 +/- 0.4 mmol/L within interval training; interval/control comparison p=0.01. Within-period mean glucose was inconclusive (p=0.08). Small unmasked trial, baseline imbalance and missing sensor record; oxidative-stress markers did not improve. No blanket superiority to all continuous exercise."},"citation_key":"stage2-ref-karstoft","canonical_reference":{"author_year":"Karstoft et al. (2017)","number":10,"anchor":"#pm-ref-10"}}],"sec_assessment_ref":{"id":"glycaemic-f7-assessment-v1","version":2,"sha256":"5a9e2332642abccb1d7cc7fb4f8ba330d17f0593dcafed4ac3a28c063f58d0a3"},"connected_supportive_evidence":[]}} pmId={"BRS6-FM1-PM2"} />
    
