          - label: 10.1107/S2052252526005075
            href: '#same-study-3'
            evidence_source: bounded-external-search
            directional_finding: CryoEM conformers suggest additional allosteric regulation. Catalytic-activity arguments partly reuse earlier experiments; this is not independent replication of the stability endpoint. Does not refute a stability contribution or establish that all MAT2B effects are stability alone.
            citation_key: same-study-3
            data_level: Cellular / Molecular
            assessment:
              study: Contextual structural/allosteric interpretation; challenges stability-only explanations
              population: 'Purified human enzyme, mammalian cellular or structural experiments as specified in the source appraisal; no dietary human intervention.'
              result: CryoEM conformers suggest additional allosteric regulation. Catalytic-activity arguments partly reuse earlier experiments; this is not independent replication of the stability endpoint. Does not refute a stability contribution or establish that all MAT2B effects are stability alone.
              effect_magnitude: CryoEM conformers suggest additional allosteric regulation. Catalytic-activity arguments partly reuse earlier experiments; this is not independent replication of the stability endpoint. Does not refute a stability contribution or establish that all MAT2B effects are stability alone.
              evidence_summary: CryoEM conformers suggest additional allosteric regulation. Catalytic-activity arguments partly reuse earlier experiments; this is not independent replication of the stability endpoint. Does not refute a stability contribution or establish that all MAT2B effects are stability alone.
