    <ScientificFinding finding={{"id":"PM3-F4","finding_label":"Biochemical provenance: methionine regeneration","finding_summary":"Folate and betaine remethylation regenerate methionine upstream of MAT-dependent SAMe formation; choline can contribute through betaine.","finding_interpretation":"This establishes connected precursor provision. It does not make folate, betaine or choline MAT reactants, demonstrate that more intake raises synthesis, or resolve a donor-inadequacy constraint on MAT capacity.","finding_statement":"Folate and betaine remethylation regenerate methionine upstream of MAT-dependent SAMe formation; choline can contribute through betaine.","presentation":"mechanistic-basis","fm_rollup":false,"synthesised_evidence_confidence":"not-yet-scored","synthesis":"Existing reviewed PM1-F1, PM2-F1/PM2-F2 and PM3-F1 establish the successive reaction identities. Folate provides 5-methyltetrahydrofolate for B12-dependent methionine synthase, while betaine supplies the alternative BHMT reaction, predominantly in liver and kidney. Choline oxidation can supply betaine. The regenerated methionine is available to the MAT reaction. Evidence supports the route, without requiring each donor to act directly on MAT.","synthesis_limitations":"Tissue expression, alternative methionine supply and pathway compensation limit generalisation. SAMe and SAM:SAH are pool-state measurements rather than isolated synthesis rates. No established limiting effect on MAT capacity or nutrient-replete intake benefit is claimed.","evidence_considered":[{"label":"Froese et al. (2019)","citation_key":"froese_vitamin_2019","href":"/docs/papers/BRAIN-Diet-References#froese_vitamin_2019","data_level":"Mechanistic","evidence_source":"repository-inherited","directional_finding":"Establishes folate/B12 remethylation and placement before MAT synthesis; reviewed on PM1-F1.","canonical_reference":{"author_year":"Froese et al. (2019)","number":7,"anchor":"#pm-ref-7"}},{"label":"Obeid (2013)","citation_key":"obeid_metabolic_2013","href":"/docs/papers/BRAIN-Diet-References#obeid_metabolic_2013","data_level":"Mechanistic","evidence_source":"repository-inherited","directional_finding":"Establishes betaine donation and choline provision in connected remethylation; reviewed on PM2-F1/F2.","canonical_reference":{"author_year":"Obeid (2013)","number":8,"anchor":"#pm-ref-8"}},{"label":"Bailey et al. (2021)","citation_key":"bailey_human_mat2a_2021","href":"/docs/papers/BRAIN-Diet-References#bailey_human_mat2a_2021","data_level":"Mechanistic","evidence_source":"repository-inherited","directional_finding":"Establishes methionine and ATP use in human MAT2A; reviewed on PM3-F1.","canonical_reference":{"author_year":"Bailey et al. (2021)","number":1,"anchor":"#pm-ref-1"}},{"label":"Evans et al. (2002)","citation_key":"evans_betaine_2002","href":"/docs/papers/BRAIN-Diet-References#evans_betaine_2002","data_level":"Cellular / Molecular","evidence_source":"repository-inherited","directional_finding":"Human BHMT reaction identity; supports betaine-to-methionine provision, not dietary MAT responsiveness.","canonical_reference":{"author_year":"Evans et al. (2002)","number":9,"anchor":"#pm-ref-9"}},{"label":"Salvi and Gadda (2013)","citation_key":"salvi_choline_2013","href":"/docs/papers/BRAIN-Diet-References#salvi_choline_2013","data_level":"Cellular / Molecular","evidence_source":"repository-inherited","directional_finding":"Choline oxidation through betaine aldehyde to betaine; supports route identity, not MAT flux.","canonical_reference":{"author_year":"Salvi and Gadda (2013)","number":10,"anchor":"#pm-ref-10"}}],"connected_supportive_evidence":[],"informs":[],"evidence_dependency":["Bailey et al. (2021) is reused from PM3-F1 to identify MAT substrate use; it is not independent supply-chain or dietary-response evidence."],"sec_assessment_ref":{"id":"same-pm3-f4-assessment-v1","version":2,"sha256":"8a51c38cc9237b29c033c9ac50af12a385255ca2c1d961f4bb20e1647a3411e5"}}} pmId={"BRS2-FM1-PM3"} />
    
