    <ScientificFinding finding={{"id":"PM3-F5","finding_label":"MAT2B and MAT2A stability","evidence_dependency":["Bailey et al. (2021) is also used by PM3-F1 and PM3-F4. Reuse for the stability proposition is not independent replication."],"finding_statement":"MAT2B association can preserve MAT2A protein or catalytic stability in purified-human-enzyme and mammalian-cell experiments. This supports a stability contribution to enzyme regulation, not an exclusive explanation of MAT2B action or a demonstrated increase in human SAMe synthesis flux.","finding_summary":"MAT2B association can preserve MAT2A protein or catalytic stability in purified-human-enzyme and mammalian-cell experiments. This supports a stability contribution to enzyme regulation, not an exclusive explanation of MAT2B action or a demonstrated increase in human SAMe synthesis flux.","synthesis":"Purified-enzyme activity decay and mammalian-cell perturbation/rescue support a stability contribution, with non-identical endpoints. Additional allosteric/catalytic regulation remains possible.","synthesis_limitations":"Partial cross-model corroboration does not quantify MAT2B-dependent stability or SAMe flux in the human brain. Does not establish that stability is the only MAT2B mechanism: allosteric/catalytic interpretations remain relevant. No dietary methionine, folate, betaine, choline or ADHD intervention effect was assessed.","synthesised_evidence_confidence":"not-yet-scored","evidence_considered":[{"label":"10.1021/acs.biochem.1c00672","href":"/docs/papers/BRAIN-Diet-References#bailey_human_mat2a_2021","evidence_source":"bounded-external-search","directional_finding":"Purified human MAT2A lost activity during substrate-free incubation at 37 C; MAT2B preserved activity. Coupled phosphate and direct LC-MS assays distinguish stability from steady-state kinetic effects. Activity half-life about 2.3 minutes without MAT2B; activity retained over the 120-minute experiment with MAT2B. Technical repeats do not 