rs from purified-enzyme activity decay. Mostly representative blots with two or three repeats; no pooled half-life or universal flux effect is claimed. Later tumour/diet experiments do not establish a nutritional PM recommendation.","limitations":"Partial cross-model corroboration does not quantify MAT2B-dependent stability or SAMe flux in the human brain. Does not establish that stability is the only MAT2B mechanism: allosteric/catalytic interpretations remain relevant. No dietary methionine, folate, betaine, choline or ADHD intervention effect was assessed. Scite full text; cell perturbation/rescue Results and cycloheximide-chase Methods appraised"},"canonical_reference":{"author_year":"10.1038/s41419-024-07093-8","number":11,"anchor":"#pm-ref-11"}},{"label":"10.1107/S2052252526005075","href":"#same-study-3","evidence_source":"bounded-external-search","directional_finding":"CryoEM conformers suggest additional allosteric regulation. Catalytic-activity arguments partly reuse earlier experiments; this is not independent replication of the stability endpoint. Does not refute a stability contribution or establish that all MAT2B effects are stability alone.","citation_key":"same-study-3","data_level":"Cellular / Molecular","assessment":{"study":"Contextual structural/allosteric interpretation; challenges stability-only explanations","population":"Purified human enzyme, mammalian cellular or structural experiments as specified in the source appraisal; no dietary human intervention.","result":"CryoEM conformers suggest additional allosteric regulation. Catalytic-activity arguments partly reuse earlier experiments; this is not independent replication of the stability endpoint. Does not refute a stability contribution or establish that all MAT2B effects are stability alone.","effect_magnitude":"CryoEM conformers suggest additional allosteric regulation. Catalytic-activity arguments partly reuse earlier experiments; this is not independent replication of the stability endpo