    <summary>Stage 2A/2B dietary-target assessment — 23 October 2026</summary>
    
    **REVIEW REQUIRED.** MAT conversion of methionine and ATP to SAM.
    
    Methionine and reaction metals are already recorded. Historical No fields on metals cannot be silently reversed because extra-intake benefit is absent or because a structure contains the metal. Assess supply/homeostasis against the same MAT dependency separately; preserve every old decision. Dietary protein duplicates a delivery category and is flagged, not removed.
    
    **New implementation:** 0 dietary-input admissions (0 completed Unset candidates), 0 practices, 0 biochemical participants, 0 unscored Findings. Existing accepted inputs, source assessments, mission, KCs, Phenome relationships and scores are retained.
    
    **Source-to-claim boundary:** [Assessment source](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26858410/). Stop after adjudicating the stated material candidate and tracing supported delivery. Keep uncertain specificity, formulation, anatomical or measurement links explicit; no negative evidence is inferred from incomplete retrieval.
    
    </details>
