    ### PM-local source records
    
    <p id="same-study-1"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.biochem.1c00672">10.1021/acs.biochem.1c00672</a>. Supporting experimental stability evidence. Scite full text; enzyme-assay Methods, inhibition, binding and stability Results appraised</p>
    
    <p id="same-study-2"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41419-024-07093-8">10.1038/s41419-024-07093-8</a>. Independent partial corroboration of protein stability. Scite full text; cell perturbation/rescue Results and cycloheximide-chase Methods appraised</p>
    
    <p id="same-study-3"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1107/S2052252526005075">10.1107/S2052252526005075</a>. Contextual structural/allosteric interpretation; challenges stability-only explanations. Scite full-text conformational Results, Discussion and construct Methods appraised</p>
    
    <p id="same-study-4"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.biochem.0c00998">10.1021/acs.biochem.0c00998</a>. Contradictory substrate-order model; contextual to stability. Scite full-text human MAT2A kinetic Results appraised</p>
    
    <PmCuratedReferences pmId="BRS2-FM1-PM3" />
    
  actual: |-
    ---
    title: SAMe Synthesis
    pm_id: BRS2-FM1-PM3
    mission: >-
      Maintain methionine adenosyltransferase capacity to convert methionine and ATP
      into SAMe, sustaining the methyl-donor pool used by downstream
      methyltransferases.
    parent_fm: BRS2(FM1)
    parent_brs: BRS2
    evidence_status: stage-2b-dietary-addressability
    summary: >-
      Methionine adenosyltransferase forms S-adenosylmethionine from methionine and
      ATP. Magnesium and potassium ions coordinate that ATP-dependent catalysis.
      This reaction supplies the methyl donor used by many later enzymes. Upstream
      methionine regeneration and later methyl-transfer reactions remain separate
      processes. Circulating SAMe and the SAM:SAH ratio describe pool balance rather
      than synthesis speed.
    kc_applicability_adjudications:
      - kc_id: BRS2(KC2)
        ikc_id: BRS2(KC2)
        arm_id: methionine-cysteine-sulfur-amino-acid-pool
        applicability_proposition: >-
          Inadequacy of the shared methionine and cysteine pool constrains
          MAT-dependent SAMe synthesis capacity.
        disposition: unresolved
        established_links:
          - Methionine is the direct amino-acid substrate of MAT (PM3-F1).
          - >-
            Methionine requirement and connected supply remain established; dietary
            mixed methyl-deficiency results and SAM abundance do not isolate an
            additional KC2 constraint.
          - >-
            Methionine requirement and connected supply remain established; dietary
            mixed methyl-deficiency results and SAM abundance do not isolate an
            additional KC2 constraint.
        inferred_links:
          - >-
            A context-specific limitation beyond the independently recorded
            methionine substrate provision, with pool scope, compensation and SAM
            production/consumption distinguished.
        evidence_source:
          finding_ids:
            - PM3-F1
            - PM3-IC1
          citation_keys:
            - bailey_human_mat2a_2021
            - murray_crystallography_2016
            - corrillero_bravo_analysis_2022
        rationale: >-
          Remove the old universal human-MAT-flux gate. Supported animal/molecular
          triangulation is permissible. This corpus still does not establish a
          further distinct sulfur-pool limitation beyond methionine provision.
        evidence_gap: >-
          A context-specific limitation beyond the independently recorded methionine
          substrate provision, with pool scope, compensation and SAM
          production/consumption distinguished.
        review_record: system/kc-unresolved-decisions-reconciliation.md
      - kc_id: BRS2(KC1)
        ikc_id: BRS2(KC1)
        arm_id: upstream-methionine-regeneration
        applicability_proposition: >-
          KC1 contributes upstream methyl-group supply to methionine regeneration
          used by PM3.
        disposition: established
        applicability_mode: supported-upstream-supply
        relationship_type: supported-upstream-supply
        established_links:
          - Folate/B12-dependent methionine synthase regenerates methionine.
          - >-
            Betaine/BHMT regenerates methionine; choline oxidation can supply
            betaine.
          - MAT uses methionine and ATP.
        inferred_links:
          - The extent of donor availability limiting MAT flux is unresolved.
        evidence_source:
          finding_ids:
            - PM3-F4
            - PM3-F1
          citation_keys: &ref_0
            - froese_vitamin_2019
            - obeid_metabolic_2013
            - evans_betaine_2002
            - salvi_choline_2013
        rationale: >-
          Admit supported upstream supply, not conditional constraint. Tissue
          expression, alternative supply and compensation bound the route;
          pool-state markers do not measure MAT flux.
    cofactors:
      - Magnesium ions (Mg²⁺)
      - Potassium ions (K⁺)
    intervention_dominance: Diet-Supported
    intervention_breakdown: Food-State Leaning
    timing_specific: 'No'
    dose_sensitivity: >-
      Methionine is a reaction substrate, but no human dietary dose-response for
      MAT-dependent SAMe synthesis is established.
    references:
      - >-
        [Bailey et al. (2021) — Human MAT2A ordered kinetic
        mechanism](/docs/papers/BRAIN-Diet-References#bailey_human_mat2a_2021)
      - >-
