            data_level: Mechanistic
          - index: 2
            label: Corrillero Bravo et al. (2022)
            citation_key: corrillero_bravo_analysis_2022
            href: /docs/papers/BRAIN-Diet-References#corrillero_bravo_analysis_2022
            data_level: Human Mechanistic
      - target_phenome: Emotional Regulation
        relationship_type: indirect
        confidence: low-medium
        evidence_level: mechanistic
        evidence_confidence: low
        rationale: >-
          SAMe-dependent methylation is biologically relevant to downstream
          neurotransmitter and membrane chemistry, but the attached mood-disorder
          review concerns exogenous SAMe and combined folate/B12 treatment rather
          than endogenous MAT activity or SAMe synthesis flux
          {{cite:cicero_combined_2022}}. It therefore does not directly demonstrate
          that this PM modulates Emotional Regulation; the relationship remains an
