      - atom_id: PM3-DIT-5
        dietary_input: true
        dietary_input_note: "Dietary applicability is already admitted in the Direct/Derived section. This does not establish ordinary-food equivalence, a quantitative requirement, extra-intake benefit or independent supply of a derived product."
        input: Dietary protein
        input_type: substrate provision
        biological_role: >-
          Provides methionine through protein digestion and amino-acid absorption;
          methionine is the direct amino-acid substrate for MAT-dependent SAMe
          synthesis.
        evidence_source:
          finding_ids:
            - PM3-F1
          citation_keys:
            - fao_diaas_2013
        evidence_limitation: >-
          Dietary protein provides digestible methionine, but this does not
          establish that increasing protein or methionine intake increases
          MAT-dependent SAMe synthesis in humans. DIAAS evaluates sulfur amino acids
          as methionine + cysteine.
      - atom_id: PM3-KC1-UPSTREAM-1
        dietary_input: true
        dietary_input_note: "Accepted upstream dietary constituent provision is distinct from the pool/constraint reference. Existing role, conditional scope and limitations remain unchanged."
        input: Vitamin B9 (folate)
        input_type: supported upstream supply
        biological_role: >-
          Folate supplies 5-methyltetrahydrofolate to [PM1 — Folate/B12-dependent
          remethylation](/docs/biological-targets/brs2/fm1/brs2-fm1-pm1-folate-b12-dependent-homocysteine-remethylation),
          regenerating methionine that PM3 can use to form SAMe.
