  actual: |-
    ---
    title: GABA Synthesis Capacity
    pm_id: BRS1-FM4-PM9
    mission: >-
      Maintain sufficient glutamate decarboxylase capacity, and sufficient PLP
      cofactor to support it, so GABA can be synthesised from glutamate.
    parent_fm: BRS1(FM4)
    parent_brs: BRS1
    summary: >-
      The brain makes GABA, its main calming transmitter, by converting glutamate
      with an enzyme that needs the active form of vitamin B6. That reaction
      supplies GABA for later inhibitory signalling. Vitamin B6 in food is the
      dietary route to the cofactor, and it mainly affects reserve capacity rather
      than everyday output.
    cofactors:
      - Pyridoxal 5′-phosphate (PLP; active vitamin B6 cofactor)
    dietary_input_traceability:
      - atom_id: PM9-DIT-1
        dietary_input: false
        dietary_input_note: "Accepted intracellular/endogenous participant; no dietary supply relationship is admitted for this entry in this PM."
        input: Glutamate
        input_type: substrate
        biological_role: Substrate for GAD-dependent GABA synthesis
        evidence_source:
          finding_ids:
            - PM9-F1
          citation_keys:
            - martin_regulation_1993
        evidence_limitation: >-
          The evidence establishes glutamate as the GAD substrate, not that dietary
          glutamate or protein controls neuronal glutamate availability or human
          brain GABA synthesis.
      - atom_id: PM9-DIT-2
        dietary_input: null
        dietary_input_note: "Direct-section admission conflicts with the explicit limitation excluding dietary PLP provision. B6 precursor supply remains a separate accepted relationship."
        dietary_input_flags: ["section-supply-contradiction"]
        input: Pyridoxal 5′-phosphate (PLP; active vitamin B6 cofactor)
        input_type: cofactor
        biological_role: Required cofactor for GAD-dependent conversion of glutamate to GABA
        evidence_source:
          finding_ids:
            - PM9-F1
          citation_keys:
            - martin_regulation_1993
        evidence_limitation: >-
          The evidence establishes PLP dependence of GAD, but not dietary PLP
          provision or an intake-to-synthesis response in humans.
      - atom_id: PM9-DIT-3
        dietary_input: true
        dietary_input_note: "Accepted dietary provision or constituent supply relationship; no efficacy or quantity claim added."
        input: Vitamin B6
        input_type: cofactor precursor
        biological_role: >-
          Provides dietary B6 vitamers that pyridoxal kinase converts to PLP, the
          cofactor required for GAD-dependent GABA synthesis
        evidence_source:
          finding_ids:
