          and emotional regulation. Human studies link GABA concentrations in
          relevant brain regions with impulsivity and aggression
          {{cite:ende_impulsivity_2016}}, supporting the relevance of GABA biology
          to Emotional Regulation. However, these studies measure GABA concentration
          rather than synthesis rate {{cite:mason_decrease_2001,manor_rate_1996}},
          and direct human evidence connecting GABA synthesis capacity itself with
          Emotional Regulation is currently lacking.
