    hide_title: true
    scientific_findings_intro: >-
      Enzyme evidence distinguishes largely cofactor-saturated GAD67, which sustains
      basal synthesis, from a recruitable GAD65 pool: PLP availability can therefore
      influence reserve synthesis capacity rather than simply determine the resting
      rate. [[1]](#pm-ref-1) Recombinant human pyridoxal-kinase studies show
      metal-dependent PLP formation under specified assay conditions, but do not
      establish physiological zinc limitation. [[2]](#pm-ref-2) [[4]](#pm-ref-4)
      This evidence supports biochemical dependence, not selective enhancement of
      brain GABA production from additional vitamin B6 or zinc intake.
